# GRAVEYARD backend — example environment variables
#
# Copy this file to .env and adjust values for your local setup.
# Load with: node --env-file=.env dist/server.js
#
# No dotenv package is required; --env-file is built into Node.js 20.6+.

# TCP port the server listens on. Integer 1–65535. Default: 3002
PORT=3002

# Host/IP the server binds to. Default: 127.0.0.1 (loopback only)
# Use 0.0.0.0 to accept connections on all interfaces.
HOST=127.0.0.1

# Pino log level. One of: fatal error warn info debug trace silent. Default: info
LOG_LEVEL=info

# Path to the SQLite database file. The directory is created automatically.
# Use :memory: for an ephemeral in-process database (tests only).
# Default: ./data/graveyard.sqlite
DATABASE_PATH=./data/graveyard.sqlite

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Opt-in local worker (separate process: `pnpm run worker`). Everything below is
# commented out on purpose: the API never starts a worker and the worker does
# nothing unless GRAVEYARD_WORKER_ENABLED is exactly 1. It runs ONLY the
# operator-prepared fixtures listed in the catalog; any other repository URL is
# refused (nothing is cloned or run). Needs Docker and a local node:22-alpine.
# See backend/README.md "Local worker" for the catalog format and the limits.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# GRAVEYARD_WORKER_ENABLED=1
# GRAVEYARD_FIXTURES_ROOT=C:\absolute\path\to\fixtures
# GRAVEYARD_STAGING_ROOT=C:\absolute\path\to\staging
# GRAVEYARD_NPM_CACHE_DIR=C:\absolute\path\to\npm-cache
# GRAVEYARD_FIXTURE_CATALOG=C:\absolute\path\to\catalog.json
# GRAVEYARD_WORKER_ID=worker-1
# GRAVEYARD_WORKER_POLL_MS=2000
# GRAVEYARD_WORKER_RECOVER_MS=30000
# GRAVEYARD_WORKER_BATCH=5
# GRAVEYARD_WORKER_SHUTDOWN_MS=45000
# off | kiro-v2 | kiro-v3. Anything but off sends bounded, redacted evidence to Kiro's service.
# GRAVEYARD_WORKER_AGENTS=off
#
# Optional GitHub flow (backend/README.md "GitHub repository flow"). Setting any of these turns it on
# and requires the catalog, runs root and the three GITHUB_EGRESS variables. Without them the worker is
# fixtures-only and no egress guard ever attests. Pins are FULL 40-hex commits chosen by the operator.
# Needs an operator-provisioned internal network and one proxy container per host (see the README).
# GRAVEYARD_GITHUB_CATALOG=C:\absolute\path\to\github-pins.json
# Optional, exactly 1 or 0 (default off). 1 lets a URL in neither catalog be inspected at its resolved HEAD
# (source-inspected only: nothing is installed, built or run, nothing goes to Kiro). It makes the pin
# catalog above optional; all other variables in this group stay required.
# GRAVEYARD_GITHUB_ALLOW_UNPINNED=0
# GRAVEYARD_GITHUB_RUNS_ROOT=C:\absolute\path\to\runs
# GRAVEYARD_GITHUB_GIT_IMAGE=alpine/git:2.47.2
# GRAVEYARD_GITHUB_EGRESS_NETWORK=graveyard-gh-net
# GRAVEYARD_GITHUB_EGRESS_PROXY_CONTAINER=graveyard-gh-proxy
# GRAVEYARD_GITHUB_EGRESS_PROXY_URL=http://10.201.5.10:3128
# Optional, all three or none (without them a repository in the supported class is reported as not runnable):
# GRAVEYARD_REGISTRY_EGRESS_NETWORK=graveyard-npm-net
# GRAVEYARD_REGISTRY_EGRESS_PROXY_CONTAINER=graveyard-npm-proxy
# GRAVEYARD_REGISTRY_EGRESS_PROXY_URL=http://10.202.5.10:3128
# Optional, exactly 1 or 0 (default off). 1 runs `npm run build` and `npm run test` of a PINNED repository
# whose package.json declares scripts and fits the narrow profile (backend/README.md "npm scripts mode").
# Needs the pin catalog and all three GRAVEYARD_REGISTRY_EGRESS_* variables. No Kiro, no patch, no repair.
# GRAVEYARD_GITHUB_NPM_SCRIPTS=0
# Optional, exactly 1 or 0 (default 0). Requires GRAVEYARD_GITHUB_NPM_SCRIPTS=1. Also accepts flat unscoped devDependencies
# (installed with --include=dev --ignore-scripts); unchanged size limits apply (backend/README.md "Dev dependencies").
# GRAVEYARD_GITHUB_NPM_DEV_DEPENDENCIES=0

